; claude: networking, from scratch, for teaching: one idea per module,
; each .mli with its diagram, worked example and references, like
; physics/, audio/ and ai/ (see networking/README.md,
; plan_dependencies_remaining.md section 2, and
; plan_networking_teaching.md for the games' part). Pure OCaml, no
; sockets: a message is bytes in, bytes out, so the tests need no
; network and every backend, the web one included, can use them. The
; sockets are networking/unix/.
;
; A library per subdirectory, protocols/ then netcode/ on it; this one,
; 'networking', has no module of its own: it is both, for what says
; (libraries networking). Unwrapped, or dune would make it a module
; Networking.
(library
 (name networking)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules)
 (libraries networking_protocols networking_netcode)
)
